446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 310 0 R
/E (Our system takes configurations from different network vendors and uses AI-assisted parsing to understand their different command structures. It extracts the security information, converts it into a common security model, and checks it against frameworks such as CIS, NIST, STIG, and ISO 27001. The compliance engine marks each control as PASS or FAIL and assigns a severity level to the findings. These results are then turned into a security report showing the device, compliance score, failed controls, evidence, and recommended fixes for each device. The key feature is the Adaptive Training Loop. If the AI finds an unfamiliar configuration it cannot understand, an administrator can map it to its security meaning. The system learns this mapping and reuses it when similar configurations appear in the future.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
